{
  "_about": [
    "The Problem Database's query bank (docs/problem-db/README.md). problems-collect.mjs searches with it, problems-process.mjs scores with it.",
    "Problems only: how people complain or ask for a fix, never a product or a product idea.",
    "patterns: how people complain or ask, per language. kind: complaint, need, question or struggle. search: false keeps a pattern out of the searches (it still counts when found in a post). '...' stands for a few words in between ('weet iemand hoe ik ... kan oplossen').",
    "areas: the parts of life. keywords go with the patterns in text searches (Reddit, Threads); topics are searched as they are on the video platforms (TikTok, YouTube), whose comments hold the complaints; subreddits are searched with the patterns alone.",
    "general: subreddits of no single area, searched with the patterns alone. signals: words that score a problem, never searched. countries: words that say where a post is from (a guess).",
    "Add a line anywhere: test/problems.bank.test.mjs checks the file (every area in every language, no duplicates, valid subreddit names). Lower case or not does not matter."
  ],
